"""The parts catalog, one entry each: what it is, where it comes from, how it is drawn.

A Part carries its schematic symbol, footprint, the Value text the schematic shows, and the manufacturer
data PCBWay needs (stamped on the symbol at placement, so a symbol and its part can never disagree).
Values of passives parse into a Quantity for checks. ``hand`` marks through-hole parts to be soldered
by hand at PCBWay. Notes are the PCBWay 'Your notes' column: alternates, cautions.

Provenance: the former parts_table.py (checked against manufacturer drawings and Digi-Key 2026-09-06)
and lcsc.py (JLCPCB catalogue snapshot 2026-09-05), merged into this file 2026-09-07. Footprint fit notes
stay with each entry. Generated once from those tables; edit by hand from here on.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

from .parts import Part, Quantity  # noqa: F401

